						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg15259#msg15259"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg15259#msg15259">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2368 on:</b> March 07, 2005, 04:06:08 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">just tired of seeing them placed together attached at the hip.</div>They <span style="text-decoration: underline;">just are</span>, thats the way its been for a long time now and probably will be til EQ ends. Its not a set up I would enjoy but obviously it works very well for them.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">I know EiE has been trying to recruit (clerics and bards mainly) within the ranks of other guilds</div>Even though its shitty if/when an officer does it, it happens. <br />Ive had two of my clerics come to me about Non-friend recruiters sending them tells just this past week.  <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cwm13.gif" alt="cwm13" border="0" /><br />But where else are they supposed to find well geared, raid experienced people at? Wal-mart?<br />I&#039;m not saying its right, and I personally wont poach directly from other guilds, because its simply underhanded...<br />but really, who else is out there at this point worth recruiting that doesnt have a tag over their head?<br />cross server trannies and ebayers?
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
